@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/driver#> .
@prefix courier: <http://example.org/orexis/courier#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .

<> a orexis:BeliefGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is
<> orexis:ownedBy :dispatcher .    # and whose it is — said here, never by the file's name

#  THE TWO DELIVERIES AS POSED, one on each grid: each van at the foot of its grid's first column,
#  its parcel one cell up it, owed at the top — five steps each, a drive, the pick, two drives, the
#  drop — and the driver aboard van A. The only file here the runtime never reloads: from the first
#  boot on, where the vans, the parcels and the driver stand is the agent's belief, rewritten by its
#  own actions.

:driver courier:aboard :van_a .

:van_a courier:x 0 ; courier:y 0 .
:parcel_a courier:x 0 ; courier:y 1 .

:van_b courier:x 10 ; courier:y 0 .
:parcel_b courier:x 10 ; courier:y 1 .
